config WTK_USB_INSERT_DETECT
	bool "Wingtech USB insertion detection (Doogee S88 Pro, PARTIAL BATCH)"
	default n
	help
	  ONE function out of five, and that has to be said at the top.

	  The factory translation unit has five of them, in a contiguous run right
	  after the end of `mt5725`:

	    ffffff8008ace8f0 T usb_insert_online                 <- THIS ONE, 20 bytes
	    ffffff8008ace904 t usb_insert_detect_probe           (596 bytes)
	    ffffff8008aceb58 t usb_insert_detect_remove          (8 bytes)
	    ffffff8008aceb60 t usb_insert_detect_thread_kthread
	    ffffff8009385a80 t usb_insert_detect_init            (in .init.text)

	  THERE IS ONLY ONE HERE, and the reason is explicit: `mt5725` calls it,
	  and without it that driver -- complete in every other respect -- does not
	  link.  The other four were not written, and they are not postponed out of
	  difficulty: they simply were not needed to close the mt5725 link.

	  THE DRIVER DOES NOT WORK LIKE THIS: with no `probe` nobody registers
	  anything and `usb_insert_online` reads an `int` nobody updates, so it
	  always returns the same value.  It is DECLARED SCAFFOLDING for the link,
	  not a driver, and it is `select`ed by MTK_MT5725_WLS_SUPPORT exactly for
	  that -- turning it on by itself makes no sense.
